:: Millers Babysitting Kitchen Help Kayden Homework [nobr]

/* Intro */
You spy <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span> sitting at the kitchen counter looking absolutely miserable as he does his schoolwork. <span style="Color: Yellow">He looks like he is about to rip his skin off or jump into oncoming traffic with how bored he is, glancing up at you with a look of utter defeat.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Daddy said I have to get it done before he gets home or he’ll spank my butt.”</span> He sighs, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Normally <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">ZayZay</span> helps us, but since they’re gone I gotta figure all this out! It’s impossible!”</span> He throws his hands up and slumps back in his chair pouting. You glance over at his homework and find that, despite his protests, it is a pretty simple assignment. <br>

    <<set _ad to [
        {
            Name: "Player",
            State: {
                Mouth: "Happy",
            },
        },
        {
            Name: "OC Kayden",
            State: {
                Outfit: "Everyday",
                Mouth: "Frown",
                Eyes: "Tired",
            },
        },
    ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

So, you sit down next to him and offer to help, though explain that you won’t be doing it for him, just helping him where he needs it. He glances up at you, obviously not wanting just help, but sighs and accepts it. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span> is actually a pretty smart kid and he is able to figure it out pretty easily, but the absolute boredom of it all is his real issue. <br>
<br>
Thankfully, you are able to think of a few ways to make it more exciting. <span style="Color: LightGreen">Changing the context of the problems, offering him rewards for success, even a round of giving him a ‘spanking’ when he failed, which was more or less some playful taps on his clothed rear that make him giggle and cause you to chase him around. You turned it into so much of a game that he looks almost disappointed when his schoolwork is all done.</span> <br>
<<set $OCKaydenBabysitHomework to 1>>
<<socialChange "Kayden" 3 1>>
<<needChange "Fun" 3>>
<span style="color:green">+Kayden Fun</span><br>
<<set $HangOutNeed.Fun += 5>>
<span style="color:green">+Kayden Comfort</span><br>
<<set $HangOutNeed.Comfort += 5>>
<br>
